<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-increasing-and-decreasing-functions" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Increasing and Decreasing Functions</title>
  
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Derivatives provide a lot of information about the shape of a function's graph. First, we will analyze whether functions are increasing or decreasing.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  
  <subsection xml:id="subsec-increasing-decreasing-functions">
    <title>Increasing and Decreasing Functions</title>
    
    <p>
      Recall what it means for a function to be increasing or decreasing.
    </p>
    
    <sidebyside width="45%">
      <image width="100%">
        <latex-image>
          \begin{tikzpicture}
          \begin{axis}[
          axis lines=middle,
          xlabel=$x$, ylabel=$y$,
          xmin=-1, xmax=4,
          ymin=-1, ymax=6,
          xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty,
          domain=-1:3,
          samples=100,
          ]
          \addplot[very thick, blue, smooth] {0.1*x^3 + 0.8*x + 0.7};
          \node[blue, above right] at (axis cs:0.5,4) {Increasing};
          \end{axis}
          \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-image>
      </image>
      <image width="100%">
        <latex-image>
          \begin{tikzpicture}
          \begin{axis}[
          axis lines=middle,
          xlabel=$x$, ylabel=$y$,
          xmin=-1, xmax=4,
          ymin=-1, ymax=6,
          xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty,
          domain=-1:3,
          samples=100,
          ]
          \addplot[very thick, red, smooth] {-0.1*x^3 - 0.8*x + 4.7};
          \node[red, above right] at (axis cs:1.5,3.5) {Decreasing};
          \end{axis}
          \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-image>
      </image>
    </sidebyside>
    
    <definition>
      <title>Increasing and decreasing functions</title>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p>A function <m>f</m> is <term>increasing</term> if when <m>x</m> increases, <m>f(x)</m> increases.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>A function <m>f</m> is <term>decreasing</term> if when <m>x</m> increases, <m>f(x)</m> decreases.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </definition>
    
    <p>
      In other words,
    </p>
    <md>
      <mrow>
        \boxed{\begin{array}{c}
        \text{increasing} \ \iff x \uparrow y \uparrow \\
        \text{decreasing} \ \iff x \uparrow y \downarrow
        \end{array}}
      </mrow>
    </md>
    
    <remark>
      <p>
        Increasing and decreasing come from the perspective of reading from left to right (or, with increasing <m>x</m>).
      </p>
    </remark>
  </subsection>
  
  <subsection xml:id="subsec-increasing-decreasing-test">
    <title>Increasing/Decreasing Test (Positive Derivative Implies Increasing)</title>
    
    <p>
      Increasing and decreasing directly relate to derivatives. Recall that the value of the derivative <m>f'</m> represents the slope of the tangent line of <m>f</m>. This means that,
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>If <m>f'(x) \gt 0</m>, then the tangent line has positive slope, and its graph is sloping up to the right, and so is increasing.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Similarly, if <m>f'(x) \lt 0</m>, then the tangent line has negative slope, and so <m>f</m> is decreasing.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    
    <sidebyside width="45%">
      <image width="100%">
        <latex-image>
          \begin{tikzpicture}
          \begin{axis}[
          axis lines=middle,
          xlabel=$x$, ylabel=$y$,
          xmin=-1, xmax=4,
          ymin=-1, ymax=6,
          xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty,
          domain=-1:3,
          samples=100,
          ]
          % Curve (increasing)
          \addplot[very thick, blue, smooth] {0.1*x^3 + 0.8*x + 0.7};
          \node[blue, above right] at (axis cs:0.5,4) {Increasing};
          
          % Tangent segments (longer, thicker, same color)
          % at x0 = -0.5: y = 0.875 x + 0.725
          \addplot[black!70, line width=3pt, domain=-0.9:-0.1] {0.875*x + 0.725};
          % at x0 = 0.5:  y = 0.875 x + 0.675
          \addplot[black!70, line width=3pt, domain=0.1:0.9] {0.875*x + 0.675};
          % at x0 = 1.5:  y = 1.475 x + 0.025
          \addplot[black!70, line width=3pt, domain=1.1:1.9] {1.475*x + 0.025};
          % at x0 = 2.5:  y = 2.675 x - 2.425
          \addplot[black!70, line width=3pt, domain=2.1:2.9] {2.675*x - 2.425};
          
          \end{axis}
          \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-image>
      </image>
      <image width="100%">
        <latex-image>
          \begin{tikzpicture}
          \begin{axis}[
          axis lines=middle,
          xlabel=$x$, ylabel=$y$,
          xmin=-1, xmax=4,
          ymin=-1, ymax=6,
          xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty,
          domain=-1:3,
          samples=100,
          ]
          % Curve (decreasing)
          \addplot[very thick, red, smooth] {-0.1*x^3 - 0.8*x + 4.7};
          \node[red, above right] at (axis cs:1.5,3.5) {Decreasing};
          
          % Tangent segments (longer, thicker, same color)
          % at x0 = -0.5: y = -0.875 x + 4.675
          \addplot[black!70, line width=3pt, domain=-0.9:-0.1] {-0.875*x + 4.675};
          % at x0 = 0.5:  y = -0.875 x + 4.725
          \addplot[black!70, line width=3pt, domain=0.1:0.9] {-0.875*x + 4.725};
          % at x0 = 1.5:  y = -1.475 x + 5.375
          \addplot[black!70, line width=3pt, domain=1.1:1.9] {-1.475*x + 5.375};
          % at x0 = 2.5:  y = -2.675 x + 7.825
          \addplot[black!70, line width=3pt, domain=2.1:2.9] {-2.675*x + 7.825};
          
          \end{axis}
          \end{tikzpicture}
        </latex-image>
      </image>
    </sidebyside>
    
    <theorem>
      <title>Positive derivative implies increasing</title>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p>If <m>f'(x) \gt 0</m> for all <m>x \in (a,b)</m>, then <m>f</m> is <alert>increasing</alert> on <m>(a,b)</m>.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>If <m>f'(x) \lt 0</m> for all <m>x \in (a,b)</m>, then <m>f</m> is <alert>decreasing</alert> on <m>(a,b)</m>.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>If <m>f'(x) = 0</m> for all <m>x \in (a,b)</m>, then <m>f</m> is <alert>constant</alert> on <m>(a,b)</m>.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </theorem>
    
    <p>
      In short,
    </p>
    <md>
      <mrow>
        \boxed{\begin{array}{c}
        f' \gt 0 \ \iff \text{increasing} \\
        f' \lt 0 \ \iff \text{decreasing}
        \end{array}}
      </mrow>
    </md>
    
    <p>
      Graphically, these statements are intuitively true. However, a proof requires the mean value theorem, which we will cover later on.
    </p>
  </subsection>
  
  <subsection xml:id="subsec-finding-intervals-increase-decrease">
    <title>Finding Intervals of Increase and Decrease</title>
    
    <project>
      <title>Basic Examples</title>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=4-x^2</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=-2x</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,0)</m>, decreasing: <m>(0,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=x^3-3x</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=3(x-1)(x+1)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,-1),(1,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-1,1)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=2x^3+3x^2+1</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=6x(x+1)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,-1),(0,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-1,0)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=x^2-16</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=2x</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(0,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,0)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=x^3+4x</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=3x^2+4</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,\infty)</m>, decreasing: none</p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=(x-1)^2</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=2x-2</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(1,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,1)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\frac{x^3}{3}-\frac{5x^2}{2}+4x</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=(x-1)(x-4)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,1),(4,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(1,4)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=-\frac{x^3}{3}+\frac{x^2}{2}+2x</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=-(x-2)(x+1)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-1,2)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-1),(2,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=12+x-x^2</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=1-2x</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,\frac{1}{2})</m>, decreasing: <m>(\frac{1}{2},\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
    </project>
    
    <project>
      <title>More Polynomial Examples</title>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=x^4-4x^3+4x^2</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=4x(x-1)(x-2)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(0,1),(2,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,0),(1,2)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=-\frac{x^4}{4}+x^3-x^2</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=-x(x-1)(x-2)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,0),(1,2)</m>, decreasing: <m>(0,1),(2,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=3x^4+4x^3-12x^2+2</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=12x(x-1)(x+2)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-2,0),(1,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-2),(0,1)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=2x^5-\frac{15x^4}{4}+\frac{5x^3}{3}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=5x^2(2x-1)(x-1)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,\frac{1}{2}),(1,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(\frac{1}{2},1)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=-12x^5+75x^4-80x^3</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=-60x^2(x-1)(x-4)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(1,4)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,1),(4,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=-2x^4+x^2+10</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=-2x(2x-1)(2x+1)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,-\frac{1}{2}),(0,\frac{1}{2})</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\frac{1}{2},0),(\frac{1}{2},\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\frac{x^4}{4}-\frac{8x^3}{3}+\frac{15x^2}{2}+8</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=x(x-3)(x-5)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(0,3),(5,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,0),(3,5)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
    </project>
    
    <project>
      <title>Trigonometry Examples</title>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=-2\cos x-x</m> on <m>[0,2\pi]</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=2\sin x-1</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(\frac{\pi}{6},\frac{5\pi}{6})</m>, decreasing: <m>(0,\frac{\pi}{6}),(\frac{5\pi}{6},2\pi)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\sqrt{2}\sin x-x</m> on <m>[0,2\pi]</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\sqrt{2}\cos x-1</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(0,\frac{\pi}{4}),(\frac{7\pi}{4},2\pi)</m>, decreasing: <m>(\frac{\pi}{4},\frac{7\pi}{4})</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\cos^2 x</m> on <m>[-\pi,\pi]</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=-2\sin x\cos x=-\sin 2x</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\frac{\pi}{2},0),(\frac{\pi}{2},\pi)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\pi,-\frac{\pi}{2}),(0,\frac{\pi}{2})</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=3\cos 3x</m> on <m>[-\pi,\pi]</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=-9\sin 3x</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\pi,-\frac{2\pi}{3}),(-\frac{\pi}{3},0),(\frac{\pi}{3},\frac{2\pi}{3})</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\frac{2\pi}{3},-\frac{\pi}{3}),(0,\frac{\pi}{3}),(\frac{2\pi}{3},\pi)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
    </project>
    
    <project>
      <title>More Examples</title>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=(x^2-4)^{1/2}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\frac{x}{\sqrt{x^2-4}}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(2,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-2)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=xe^{-x}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=e^{-x}(1-x)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,1)</m>, decreasing: <m>(1,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=3xe^x</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=3e^x(x+1)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-1,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-1)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=x^2-2\ln x</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=2x-\frac{2}{x}=\frac{2(x-1)(x+1)}{x}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(1,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(0,1)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\sqrt{x}\cdot\ln x</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\frac{\ln x+2}{2\sqrt{x}}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(\frac{1}{e^2},\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(0,\frac{1}{e^2})</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\frac{e^x}{e^{2x}+1}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\frac{e^x(1-e^{2x})}{(e^{2x}+1)^2}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,0)</m>, decreasing: <m>(0,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=x\ln x-2x+3</m> on <m>(0,\infty)</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\ln x-1</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(e,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(0,e)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=xe^{-x^2/2}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=e^{-x^2/2}(1-x^2)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-1,1)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-1),(1,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\frac{x}{x^2+1}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\frac{1-x^2}{(x^2+1)^2}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-1,1)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-1),(1,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\sqrt{x^2+4}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\frac{x}{\sqrt{x^2+4}}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(0,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,0)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\frac{5x}{x^2+1}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\frac{-5(x^2-1)}{(x^2+1)^2}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-1,1)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-1),(1,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\frac{2x}{x^2+9}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\frac{2(9-x^2)}{(x^2+9)^2}=-\frac{2(x-3)(x+3)}{(x^2+9)^2}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-3,3)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-3),(3,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=x+\frac{1}{x}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=1-\frac{1}{x^2}=\frac{x^2-1}{x^2}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\infty,-1),(1,\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-1,0),(0,1)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\frac{x-1}{x^2+3}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=-\frac{(x-3)(x+1)}{(x^2+3)^2}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-1,3)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-1),(3,\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
    </project>
    
    <project>
      <title>Advanced Examples</title>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=(2x-1)^2(x^2-9)</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=2(2x-1)(4x-9)(x+2)</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-2,\frac{1}{2}),(\frac{9}{4},\infty)</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-2),(\frac{1}{2},\frac{9}{4})</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\tan^{-1}\brac{\frac{x}{x^2+2}}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\frac{2-x^2}{x^4+5x^2+4}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-\sqrt{2},\sqrt{2})</m>, decreasing: <m>(-\infty,-\sqrt{2}),(\sqrt{2},\infty)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement><p><m>f(x)=\sqrt{9-x^2}+\sin^{-1}\brac{\frac{x}{3}}</m></p></statement>
        <hint><p><m>f'(x)=\frac{1-x}{\sqrt{9-x^2}}</m></p></hint>
        <answer><p>increasing: <m>(-3,1)</m>, decreasing: <m>(1,3)</m></p></answer>
      </task>
    </project>
  </subsection>
  
</section>